WEBVTT

00:17:59.116 --> 00:18:00.450
In the UK, it's 10 percent.

00:18:00.492 --> 00:18:03.537
And we have longer life expectancy,

00:18:03.537 --> 00:18:05.163
fewer women dying in childbirth,

00:18:05.205 --> 00:18:06.706
lower infant mortality.

00:18:06.748 --> 00:18:08.667
So clearly, something is going right.

00:18:08.708 --> 00:18:10.794
And you might say,
"The NHS is underfunded."

00:18:10.794 --> 00:18:14.256
Bump up by one or two percent.
And of course, we have universal coverage.

00:18:14.297 --> 00:18:17.092
So there's a strong argument there
for public health care,

00:18:17.092 --> 00:18:19.136
from an efficiency perspective --

00:18:19.136 --> 00:18:20.178
(Applause)

00:18:20.220 --> 00:18:21.388
AB: Thank you.

00:18:21.388 --> 00:18:22.889
(Applause)

00:18:22.931 --> 00:18:25.684
And I would respond with this,
in regards to elderly care.

00:18:25.725 --> 00:18:27.936
If you look at the crisis
of demographic aging,

00:18:27.936 --> 00:18:30.397
and elderly care
that’s coming down the line